# Local secrets for `vite dev` (workerd). Copy to `.dev.vars` — never commit it.
#
# This Worker takes TWO secrets, and BOTH are optional.
#
# TOOL_TOKEN — the shared-secret bearer fallback accepted by src/access.ts when
# no Cloudflare Access assertion is present (curl, CI, local dev). Every route
# on this Worker, including the Flue agent mounts, is behind that gate and FAILS
# CLOSED, so with neither a TOOL_TOKEN nor an Access JWT every request is 403.
# Set it locally to be able to reach the agent at all.
TOOL_TOKEN=

# Cloudflare Access verification, for the browser path. Plain vars in a deployed
# environment; set here only if you are exercising the JWT branch locally.
# ACCESS_AUD=
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=

# API_BASE_URL — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Absolute origin of a locally-running
# API Worker (e.g. http://localhost:8789), used when the `API` service binding
# does not resolve under `vite dev`. Never set in a deployed environment; no
# wrangler.jsonc env block declares it.
# API_BASE_URL=
#
# There is NO model-provider secret. Both model families are reached through the
# `AI` binding: Workers AI as `cloudflare/@cf/...` and Claude as
# `cloudflare/anthropic/...`. AI Gateway authenticates the Anthropic leg against
# Cloudflare's Unified Billing credits, so there is no Anthropic API key and no
# Anthropic account. Traffic is pinned to the named gateway in src/app.ts.
#
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY — OPTIONAL, and leaving it unset is the supported default.
#
# TypeSafe AI key for the Jev relevance filter (src/lib/jev.ts). Jev is a hosted
# classifier: after search_catalog retrieves, it scores each passage for
# relevance and for whether the passage is trying to instruct the system, and
# the weak ones are dropped before the answering model sees them.
#
# It takes TWO switches, not one. With no key here the filter returns its input
# unchanged and opens no connection. With a key but no per-conversation toggle,
# likewise — the toggle is `initialData.jevFilter`, set when a conversation is
# created (`POST /agents/catalog/:id`), never by the model.
#
# Setting it means passage text and the user's question leave Cloudflare for
# api.typesafe.ai. The passages are public catalog data. No user identity, no
# session or conversation id and no internal column goes with them.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
